+# Data artifacts
+
+The data tree separates lifecycle stages while keeping raw Parquet immutable:
+
+- `raw/` stores source material at
+  `raw/{source}/{exchange}/{symbol}/{YYYY}/{MM}.parquet` without transformation.
+- `clean/` stores validated and normalized datasets for future downstream jobs.
+- `features/` stores derived research inputs.
+- `snapshots/` stores versioned point-in-time artifacts and manifests.
+
+`ingestion.ParquetStorage` owns raw partition creation. `ingestion.DuckDBManager`
+reads Parquet directly for analytics and stores only catalog metadata and
+snapshot manifests. DuckDB is not a replacement for the raw files.
+
+Contents are ignored by Git; the `.gitkeep` files preserve the directory
+structure. Store large, sensitive, or production datasets in approved external
+storage and document lineage when data pipelines are implemented.
