+# Architecture and operating boundaries
+
+## Purpose
+
+This document records the ownership boundaries for Quant India. The folders are
+separated so research, controls, execution, and operations can evolve without
+being collapsed into a single module.
+
+## Module ownership
+
+| Module | Responsibility | State |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `config` | Configuration schemas, environment loading, and universe selection | Implemented data settings |
+| `ingestion` | Provider acquisition, normalization, validation, and raw persistence | Implemented data foundation |
+| `research` | Research contracts, factors, strategies, experiments, reports, and CLI | Implemented research platform |
+| `models` | Research model helpers and quality-factor interfaces | Research interface implemented |
+| `backtest` | Deterministic simulation, metrics, benchmarks, and validation | Implemented research platform |
+| `portfolio` | Research-only allocation and risk-contribution utilities | Implemented allocation layer |
+| `agents` | Agent coordination and decision proposals | Scaffold only |
+| `risk_kill` | Risk limits, controls, and kill-switch boundaries | Scaffold only |
+| `execution` | Broker or venue adapters after risk approval | Scaffold only |
+| `reconciliation` | Comparison of intended, accepted, and observed state | Scaffold only |
+| `orchestration` | Workflow scheduling and lifecycle coordination | Scaffold only |
+| `observability` | Logs, metrics, traces, and operational health | Scaffold only |
+| `dashboard` | Human-facing operational views | Scaffold only |
+| `reports` | Reproducible report generation and exports | Scaffold only |
+
+The `data/` tree is an artifact boundary rather than a Python package. Raw,
+clean, feature, and snapshot data are kept separate to make lineage and
+retention decisions explicit. The implemented data flow is documented in
+[`data-foundation.md`](data-foundation.md).
+
+## Data dependency direction
+
+```text
+yfinance -> ingestion normalization -> validation
+         -> immutable data/raw Parquet -> DuckDB analytical views
+```
+
+`ingestion` may depend on `config` and its own data utilities. Future research
+and backtest components should consume registered data rather than mutate raw
+files. `dashboard` and `reports` should consume observable state rather than
+mutate portfolio or execution state.
+
+## Safety invariants
+
+1. No Market or IOC order is created anywhere in the system.
+2. Execution is downstream of `risk_kill`; no execution adapter may bypass the
+   risk engine.
+3. Research and backtest code cannot be treated as live execution code without
+   an explicit, reviewed boundary.
+4. Secrets are injected through the runtime environment or an approved secret
+   manager and are never committed to the repository.
+5. Every future public function must have focused tests and documentation.
+6. The data foundation does not import or call broker, authentication,
+   execution, or risk-engine modules.
+
+These invariants are requirements for future implementation. The current data
+foundation only downloads, validates, stores, and queries historical market
+data.
