+# Research CLI guide
+
+The installed `quant-india` entry point exposes reproducible research commands:
+
+```bash
+quant-india research run --strategy momentum --prices prices.parquet --universe nifty50
+quant-india research compare --strategy momentum --prices prices.parquet --universe nifty50
+quant-india research validate --strategy momentum --prices prices.parquet \
+  --train-size 252 --test-size 63 --embargo 5
+quant-india experiments list
+quant-india report generate --strategy momentum --prices prices.parquet
+```
+
+`--prices` accepts a wide date-indexed CSV/Parquet file or canonical long-form
+files containing `date`, `symbol`, and `close`. Reports are written as JSON and
+Markdown under `reports/generated` by default. `research run` also logs the
+experiment, including benchmark results and DSR, through `ExperimentManager`.
+
+The CLI is intentionally research-only. It does not place orders or invoke
+broker, authentication, execution, risk-kill, or agent modules.
