+# ingestion
+
+The ingestion package implements the market-data boundary for Quant India. It
+contains no broker, authentication, execution, portfolio, or risk-engine code.
+
+## Public API
+
+- `YFinanceProvider` downloads daily history with bounded exponential retries.
+- `normalize_market_data()` maps provider responses to the canonical OHLCV and
+  metadata schema.
+- `MarketDataValidator` runs Pandera schema checks, completeness checks,
+  duplicate detection, OHLC integrity checks, freshness checks, and volatility
+  outlier detection.
+- `ParquetStorage` writes immutable monthly partitions under
+  `data/raw/{source}/{exchange}/{symbol}/{YYYY}/{MM}.parquet`.
+- `DuckDBManager` owns catalog tables, direct Parquet views, query helpers, and
+  immutable snapshot manifests.
+- `MarketDataIngestor` composes those pieces into a reusable symbol or universe
+  workflow.
+- `build_ingestor()` wires the components from `config.Settings`.
+
+All blocking failures raise a typed exception and carry enough context for the
+caller to log or serialize the failure. Identical partition retries are
+reported explicitly as skips; existing partitions are never overwritten.
+
+See [`docs/data-foundation.md`](../docs/data-foundation.md) for the data flow,
+canonical schema, validation behavior, DuckDB examples, and assumptions.
