+# Requirements
+
+Runtime dependencies are split by module so future packages stay close to the
+code that owns them.
+
+- `base.txt` contains shared runtime dependencies.
+- `ingestion.txt` contains DuckDB, pandas, Pandera, PyArrow, and yfinance for
+  the implemented data foundation.
+- `research.txt` contains NumPy, VectorBT, and MLflow for the research platform.
+- `<module>.txt` contains the runtime dependencies for one other architecture
+  module; those files are intentionally empty until implementation begins.
+- `dev.txt` includes the implemented ingestion and research requirements plus
+  test, lint, and local quality tooling for CI and developer environments.
+
+When adding a dependency, update the owning module file and document why it is
+needed. Do not add broker, authentication, execution, or risk-engine packages
+to the data foundation.
